    "value": "Spring Boot 4.0.0 has been officially released and is now available from Maven Central. This release is a major update, introducing several new features and breaking changes, and is built on top of Spring Framework 7. Here’s what you need to know:\n\n## How to Use Spring Boot 4.0.0 with Maven\n\nTo add Spring Boot 4.0.0 to your Maven `pom.xml`, use:\n\n```xml\n\u003cdependency\u003e\n  \u003cgroupId\u003eorg.springframework.boot\u003c/groupId\u003e\n  \u003cartifactId\u003espring-boot\u003c/artifactId\u003e\n  \u003cversion\u003e4.0.0\u003c/version\u003e\n\u003c/dependency\u003e\n```\nOr, for Spring Boot starter-parent in the POM:\n\n```xml\n\u003cparent\u003e\n  \u003cgroupId\u003eorg.springframework.boot\u003c/groupId\u003e\n  \u003cartifactId\u003espring-boot-starter-parent\u003c/artifactId\u003e\n  \u003cversion\u003e4.0.0\u003c/version\u003e\n  \u003crelativePath/\u003e \u003c!-- lookup parent from repository --\u003e\n\u003c/parent\u003e\n```\nThe full Maven coordinates and more dependencies can be found in Spring Boot's official metadata or on [Maven Central](https://search.maven.org/artifact/org.springframework.boot/spring-boot/4.0.0/jar)【3:3†source】.\n\n## Key Features and Requirements in Spring Boot 4.0\n\n- Built on Spring Framework 7.0.\n- Java 17 is the minimum required version (Java 21+ and Java 25 recommended).\n- Full modularization of the codebase, allowing smaller and more focused JARs.\n- Enhanced null safety thanks to JSpecify.\n- Auto-configuration for API Versioning in MVC/WebFlux.\n- HTTP Service Clients auto-configuration support.\n- A dedicated starter for OpenTelemetry observability.\n- Gradle 9 support (in addition to Gradle 8.x).\n- Many dependency upgrades in the broader ecosystem: e.g., Jackson 3, Hibernate 7, Tomcat 11, Jakarta EE 11, and more【3:6†source】【3:7†source】.\n\n## Migration and Breaking Changes\n\n- You should upgrade your project to Spring Boot 3.5.x first, then upgrade to 4.0.0.\n- Many deprecated classes, methods, and properties from 3.x have been removed. Review the [migration guide](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/wiki/Spring-Boot-4.0-Migration-Guide) and prepare your project accordingly.【3:5†source】【3:2†source】\n- Undertow support is removed (Servlet 6.1 baseline requirement).\n- Properties and configuration changes: you may use the `spring-boot-properties-migrator` dependency temporarily to help with property migrations.\n\nExample for the migrator:\n```xml\n\u003cdependency\u003e\n  \u003cgroupId\u003eorg.springframework.boot\u003c/groupId\u003e\n  \u003cartifactId\u003espring-boot-properties-migrator\u003c/artifactId\u003e\n  \u003cscope\u003eruntime\u003c/scope\u003e\n\u003c/dependency\u003e\n```\nBe sure to remove the migrator after you finish migration!【3:5†source】\n\nFor in-depth changes and details, refer to:\n- [Official Release Notes](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/wiki/Spring-Boot-4.0-Release-Notes)\n- [Migration Guide](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/wiki/Spring-Boot-4.0-Migration-Guide)\n- [Documentation for Spring Boot 4.x](https://docs.spring.io/spring-boot/docs/4.0.7/reference/html/)\n\nIf you have specific concerns or questions about migrating or using Spring Boot 4.0.0 in Maven, let me know!",
